 6 |     let $y: f64.stable set_to std::math::sin($x);
   |                                              ^^
 what: this is `f64.stable`, where an angle, `f64.stable[unit: std::units::angle.radians]`, is needed
 why:  trigonometry asks for an angle in radians, so a plain number is refused, and degrees are converted with `as` (D245)
